WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.680
Speaker 1: . Yesterday, we talked about the
completely bogus conspiracy theory that spread

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:10.970
like wildfire this weekend, that Joe Biden
wants to take away red meat and even plant

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:16.049
based will force plant based beer on people,
which we know of as beer as part of his climate

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:17.049
plan.

00:00:17.049 --> 00:00:22.230
And the talking point included that Joe Biden's
climate plan would reduce each American's

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.529
so-called meat allowance to four pounds of
red meat per year.

00:00:26.529 --> 00:00:27.820
We already talked about it yesterday.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:29.150
It's completely false.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.040
But that didn't stop endless tweets and TV
segments about it.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.800
Congresswoman Lauren Bobert tweeted about
it and just accepted the premises hook, line

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.800
and sinker.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.309
Donald Trump Jr. tweeted about it.

00:00:40.309 --> 00:00:46.530
And indeed, the source on this stuff was listed
on air on Fox News as the Department of Agriculture

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.850
of the University of Michigan.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:54.140
Now, as I told you yesterday, this is a study
of hypothetical changes from the University

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.950
of Michigan from last year, from before Joe
Biden even being president.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:03.980
It has nothing to do with Joe Biden's plan,
which is simply the study simply said if people

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:10.050
did X, the result on emissions would be Y
has nothing to do with Joe Biden whatsoever.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:14.910
Now, Fox News anchor John Roberts admitted
on air yesterday that he pushed a completely

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:16.150
baseless claim on Friday.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:21.479
I call this lying about Joe Biden trying to
require Americans to reduce meat consumption

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:22.690
as part of his climate plan.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:27.070
Here is the apology, which, of course, makes
no mention of the fact that there were three

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:33.630
days of news coverage and apoplectic Republicans
which were catalyzed by the pathetic segment

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.200
that John Roberts did on Friday.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.119
Here is the retraction, if you want to call
it that.

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:41.979
Speaker 7: On Friday, we told you about a
study from the University of Michigan to give

00:01:41.979 --> 00:01:45.430
some perspective on President Biden's ambitious
climate change goals.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:49.950
That research from twenty twenty found that
cutting back how much red meat people eat

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:53.850
would have a drastic impact on harmful greenhouse
gas emissions.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.680
The data was accurate, but a graphic and a
script incorrectly implied that it was part

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.880
of Biden's plan for dealing with climate change.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.810
That is not the case.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.330
Speaker 1: OK, so at least he took it back.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:10.629
But the retraction is sort of convoluted and
quick.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:14.709
It barely even really mentions what happened
and the damage is done.

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:16.099
The genie is out of the bottle.

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:17.360
You can't unring the bell.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:20.100
Very few people see the correction.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:23.020
It's much too late and it's almost the strategy.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:30.240
They will knowingly make ten ridiculous claims
about Democrats, Biden, Obama, the left.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:32.620
They know that they're false.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:38.430
Some they will get called out on one might
explode so badly that three days later they

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.820
do a take back.

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.580
But they've succeeded overall at getting the
talking points out.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:48.239
They spend hours on multiple programs all
weekend making the same accusations.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:50.730
And then on Monday you get one short retraction.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:53.650
Remember that Judge Jeanine Pirro covered
the same story.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.650
Remember these clips?

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:55.730
I played them for you yesterday.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:59.750
Speaker 8: Finally tonight, do you like red
meat?

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.000
So the cows must go?

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:07.739
Yeah, I like burgers and I like my gas powered
car, and I'm sick of China having the upper

00:03:07.739 --> 00:03:08.790
hand over us.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.080
Speaker 1: What about Judge Jeanine's retraction?

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.350
Even if she does want.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.110
It's only a weekly show.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:17.400
She's not back until the weekend.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.050
It's almost perfect.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:24.190
You tell the lie Friday afternoon, you set
off a weekend of coverage.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:28.150
You quietly retracted on Monday on one show
only.

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.640
And by then, millions of right wingers believe
that Don Jr has tweeted about it.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.019
They've all signaled, boosted it, and nothing
comes of the attempt.

00:03:37.019 --> 00:03:40.930
And it's pretty flaccid as far as an attempt
goes to correct the record.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.100
What John Roberts did was lie.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.460
And it's a retraction.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:49.540
It's convoluted, but that is what he is in
practice actually admitting to here.

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.849
And of course, we knew the story was false
all along.

00:03:51.849 --> 00:04:12.120
There just was nothing 

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:49.860
to it.

